This repository operates under a strict Dual-Licensing Model, separating open-source community rights from commercial exemptions. The SPDX composite identifier `(CERN-OHL-S-2.0 AND AGPL-3.0-or-later)` at the repository root does NOT apply uniformly to all files. Instead, it describes a composite model where specific artifact classes are governed by specific licenses, as defined below:

----------------------------------------------------------------------
1. SCOPE & ARTIFACT CLASSIFICATION MAPPING
----------------------------------------------------------------------

A. HARDWARE DESIGNS & SCHEMATICS (SPDX: CERN-OHL-S-2.0)
   - Scope: Reference PCB layouts, component placement, electrical schematics,
     Gerber files, and hardware data diode interconnect topologies.
   - Obligation: Strongly reciprocal copyleft. Any distribution of matching or
     derivative physical designs requires publishing complete Corresponding
     Source under CERN-OHL-S v2.0, unless covered by a Commercial Exemption.

B. CONTROLLER SOFTWARE, FIRMWARE & SCRIPTS (SPDX: AGPL-3.0-or-later)
   - Scope: All reference firmware drivers, NPU lifecycle hooks, evaluation scripts,
     and CI validation tools provided by FreeCuli.
   - Obligation: Strongly reciprocal copyleft across networks under GNU AGPL v3.0.

C. NORMATIVE METHODOLOGY & SPECIFICATION DOCUMENTS (Open Standard / Prior Art)
   - Scope: The RFC 2119 normative specifications (M1-M10 invariants, CTS,
     Evidence Matrix, Defensive Publication, Attack Taxonomy).
   - Standard Usage: Free for implementation verification and conformance evaluation.
   - Conformance != Code Ownership: Implementing the standard grants FreeCuli
     NO intellectual property rights over a manufacturer's proprietary design.

----------------------------------------------------------------------
2. COMMERCIAL EXEMPTION (B2B LICENSE)
----------------------------------------------------------------------
Manufacturers seeking to build compliant Zero-Cloud appliances without
releasing proprietary trade secrets, firmware, or silicon designs MUST
execute a Commercial Exemption Agreement with FreeCuli prior to commercial distribution.

Commercial exemptions provide:
  - Exemption from CERN-OHL-S v2.0 and AGPL-3.0 copyleft source-code release obligations.
  - Authorized, licensed usage of official "FreeCuli Certified" trademarks.
  - Verification & listing in the official FreeCuli Certificate Registry.

